      "correspondence": "Reduction at 1−ζ_q identifies the q shifts in the expanded Fourier variable y and replaces substitution y↦y^q by the qth power for integer series. The q shifted factors contribute −B(y^q), while the isolated factor contributes B(y^q). The q-expansion argument divides the sum of the product and the square by 1−ζ_q and expresses it as a discriminant power times a polynomial over the cyclotomic integer ring. Evaluation, cancellation and the qth power produce the integral divisibility actually used.",
      "status": "reconstructed and independently cross-reviewed",
      "review": "Independent review computed the determinant and checked all signs and powers in the full correspondence product, including both occurrences of q+1 in the total discriminant exponent."
